Tracked placeholder for episodes/retired/ — the archive.

Git does not track empty directories, so without a tracked file here this directory
would vanish at commit and the layout the store depends on would exist only on the
machine that created it.

An episode is moved here when it is retired — consolidated into a pattern episode,
superseded, or otherwise taken out of the ordinary rhyme-search set. Its content is
never deleted and never truncated: retirement is a search-visibility switch that happens
to be spelled as a file move. Ordinary retrieval globs ../active/ and never looks here;
reaching into the archive is a separate, deliberate act (`--include-retired`, or a
`fetch` by id, which is an addressed lookup rather than a search).

Why this file is NOT a README.md: inside active/ and retired/ every Markdown file IS an
episode, so the store classifies a file by its own id grammar (`episode_id_for()` in
scripts/apply_episode_delta.py) and refuses any `.md` name it does not recognize. A
placeholder that is not a `.md` file cannot be mistaken for a record.

Full policy: ../README.md and docs/EPISODE_STORE.md §7. Files arrive here only by
scripts/apply_episode_delta.py applying a `retire` op.
